cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MAD dataset audit: three undocumented taxonomy generations in the MAST failure-mode data and pipeline"
message: "If you use the MAD dataset for code-level comparison, please cite this audit alongside the dataset."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sahin"
    given-names: "Hakan"
    alias: "hknsahin97-coder"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hknsahin97-coder/mad-audit"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-08-23"
keywords:
  - multi-agent-systems
  - llm-evaluation
  - dataset-audit
  - reproducibility
  - inter-annotator-agreement
  - failure-taxonomy
abstract: >-
  An independent, reproducible audit of the MAD dataset released with
  "Why Do Multi-Agent LLM Systems Fail?" (arXiv:2503.13657). The audit shows
  that MAD_human_labelled_dataset.json carries three different generations of
  the failure taxonomy (18, 17 and 14 modes) with silently renumbered codes, so
  pooled code-level comparison against the published MAST-14 is invalid for 15
  of its 19 records. It further shows that the shipped LLM-judge prompt answers
  in a taxonomy it does not ask for, and contradicts the definitions file it
  appends to itself. Every reported number is produced by a single stdlib-only
  script that downloads the audited files itself and prints their SHA-256.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Why Do Multi-Agent LLM Systems Fail?"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.13657"
  - type: data
    title: "mcemri/MAST-Data"
    url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/mcemri/MAST-Data"
